WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:11.200
Which jobs still need a phone call after
the office imports its latest call export?

00:16.000 --> 00:23.000
Eight updates produce two callbacks for site A.
JOB-31 is a boiler visit.

00:23.000 --> 00:29.800
JOB-48 concerns a second property. Grouping by
customer would lose one of the two callbacks.

00:33.000 --> 00:40.000
JOB-34 was answered at revision two.
An earlier missed-call update arrived later.

00:40.000 --> 00:47.600
Taking the last arrival would trigger an unnecessary
callback. Sort by source revision first.

00:54.000 --> 01:00.000
Keep the latest state for each call ID.
Eight updates describe five jobs.

01:00.000 --> 01:05.500
Only then filter for requested, open callbacks.
That keeps the stale missed call off the list.

01:08.000 --> 01:14.900
Replay all eight updates twice.
Sixteen records enter the workflow.

01:19.000 --> 01:29.200
The dispatcher still sees the same two job IDs.
Repeated imports should not duplicate callbacks.

01:36.000 --> 01:42.000
A newer record marks the boiler visit complete.
Only JOB-48 remains.

01:42.000 --> 01:46.900
The other visit for this customer is still open.

01:48.500 --> 01:58.900
Remove one call ID and the execution stops at
Latest state per call, before it can produce a partial list.
